{
  "cli": [
    {
      "argv": [
        "--help"
      ],
      "case": "cli: help",
      "status": 0,
      "stderr": "",
      "stdout": "AI Account Center\n\nUsage: ai-account-center <command> [options]\n\nCommands:\n  dashboard      Open the account and usage dashboard\n  codex-auth     Save Codex logins whose usage the dashboard reads\n  antigravity    Add or sign in again to a saved Antigravity profile on Ubuntu\n  bar            Install, launch, or inspect the native account bar\n  help           Show command help\n  version        Show version and installation paths\n\nCompatibility: ccs uses the same commands; config is an alias for dashboard.\nGlobal option: --config-dir PATH selects the existing account configuration directory.\n\nExamples:\n  ai-account-center dashboard --host localhost --port 3000 --no-open\n  ai-account-center dashboard auth setup\n  ai-account-center codex-auth show\n  ai-account-center codex-auth login work\n  ai-account-center antigravity signin party\n  ai-account-center bar version\n\n"
    },
    {
      "argv": [
        "--version"
      ],
      "case": "cli: version and paths",
      "status": 0,
      "stderr": "",
      "stdout": "AI Account Center v8.10.0\nInstallation: <repo>/dist/ccs.js\nAccount configuration: <fixture-home>/.ccs\nConfig: <fixture-home>/.ccs/config.json\nLicense: MIT; derived from CCS by Tam Nhu Tran (Kai).\nRun 'ai-account-center --help' for usage information.\n"
    },
    {
      "argv": [
        "dashboard",
        "--help"
      ],
      "case": "cli: dashboard help",
      "status": 0,
      "stderr": "",
      "stdout": "\nUsage: ai-account-center dashboard [command] [options]\nCompatibility: ccs config accepts the same arguments.\n\nOpen the account and usage dashboard.\n\nCommands:\n  auth setup         Configure dashboard username and password\n  auth show          Display dashboard authentication status\n  auth disable       Disable dashboard authentication\n  usage-hub status   Show the T3 usage hub state and the URL for T3\n  usage-hub generate --stdout   Create the T3 usage hub key (shown once)\n  usage-hub rotate --stdout     Replace the T3 usage hub key\n  usage-hub off      Turn the T3 usage hub off\n  usage-snapshot set <folder>   Publish account usage for agents into <folder>\n  usage-snapshot status|off     Show or stop the agent usage snapshot\n  proxy status       Show whether the LAN HTTPS reverse proxy is trusted\n  proxy set --address <ip> --origin <https url>   Trust the LAN HTTPS proxy\n  proxy off          Stop trusting the LAN HTTPS proxy\n  store status       Show the history store state and last backup\n  store check|backup|restore <dir>   Check, back up or restore it (dashboard stopped)\n  cursor-key set|status|remove   AAC's Cursor API key (the key on stdin, never printed)\n\nOptions:\n  --port, -p PORT    Server port (default: auto-detect)\n  --host, -H HOST    Bind host (default: localhost)\n  --no-open         Start the server without opening a browser\n  --help, -h        Show this help message\n\nLinux service startup never opens a browser automatically.\n\nExamples:\n  ai-account-center dashboard --host localhost --port 3000 --no-open\n  ai-account-center dashboard auth setup\n\n"
    },
    {
      "argv": [
        "config",
        "--help"
      ],
      "case": "cli: config is the dashboard alias",
      "status": 0,
      "stderr": "",
      "stdout": "\nUsage: ai-account-center dashboard [command] [options]\nCompatibility: ccs config accepts the same arguments.\n\nOpen the account and usage dashboard.\n\nCommands:\n  auth setup         Configure dashboard username and password\n  auth show          Display dashboard authentication status\n  auth disable       Disable dashboard authentication\n  usage-hub status   Show the T3 usage hub state and the URL for T3\n  usage-hub generate --stdout   Create the T3 usage hub key (shown once)\n  usage-hub rotate --stdout     Replace the T3 usage hub key\n  usage-hub off      Turn the T3 usage hub off\n  usage-snapshot set <folder>   Publish account usage for agents into <folder>\n  usage-snapshot status|off     Show or stop the agent usage snapshot\n  proxy status       Show whether the LAN HTTPS reverse proxy is trusted\n  proxy set --address <ip> --origin <https url>   Trust the LAN HTTPS proxy\n  proxy off          Stop trusting the LAN HTTPS proxy\n  store status       Show the history store state and last backup\n  store check|backup|restore <dir>   Check, back up or restore it (dashboard stopped)\n  cursor-key set|status|remove   AAC's Cursor API key (the key on stdin, never printed)\n\nOptions:\n  --port, -p PORT    Server port (default: auto-detect)\n  --host, -H HOST    Bind host (default: localhost)\n  --no-open         Start the server without opening a browser\n  --help, -h        Show this help message\n\nLinux service startup never opens a browser automatically.\n\nExamples:\n  ai-account-center dashboard --host localhost --port 3000 --no-open\n  ai-account-center dashboard auth setup\n\n"
    },
